WEBVTT

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.980
The boy that speaks to the wind.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.090
Work as long as here?

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.140
This is a rather nice town, Ted.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.090
What do you think?

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:32.250
I think it's fine.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.080
The ocean is close, and the way the wind blows isn't bad either.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:45.360
With this wind, I can tell that my friend just might be here in this town after all.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:46.790
Heh, the wind.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.840
You're not nearly good enough to talk to the wind like I can.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.670
Heh, yeah, right.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:53.230
Quiet, Gito.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.980
This place will do just fine.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:04.050
I'm gonna eat. You'll find us a place to stay.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:08.140
You mean like a motel? Well, those cost money.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.530
I have my money, but not yours.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.630
Our situation hasn't changed, and neither has our arrangement.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:14.860
Don't tell me you've forgotten.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.700
No, you've told me a million times.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.660
No money, get a job, otherwise you're camping out.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:23.400
That's right. You're on your own. Do what you have to do.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:24.680
Yeah, yeah, I know.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.750
Ah, but you know, I'll help you with this when the time comes.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.940
Just watch, Gito. I'll get us a five-star hotel to stay in without your help.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:46.230
Oh, it's already evening.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.050
This town is the same as all the others.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:51.510
Even if I wanted to work, no one hires me because I'm a kid.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.690
If they only knew I was more powerful than anyone else they could hire.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.970
Stop underestimating me and try me!

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.230
This power, it's all going to waste!

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.900
I hate havin' to ask Jito for meal money again.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.020
My entire fortune.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.380
Two gumballs.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.610
Some dinner.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.150
Oh well.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.370
I guess I better find a place to camp out for the night.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:29.960
This place looks pretty gu-

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:35.010
There's a roof, too. Maybe I'll have a warm night for once. Huh?

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:49.110
Oh, I get it. Well, if you're just playing, can I use your secret base for the night to camp out?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:56.430
You can't stay when I want to play at the...

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.920
What? How? You avoided my jab!

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.580
I barely dodged his punches. He's so fat!

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.100
Look, kid, don't start feeling good about yourself just because you're still standing.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:20.830
Come with me for a second.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.620
Are you trying to tell me to?

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:10.630
You're a Momodo?

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:59.360
Wanna do should we go get the owners of our books and fight fighting anyway good. I'm wiped out to the truth

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.190
My name is Ted. What's yours?

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.110
My name is Zatch Bell.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:06.460
Nice to meet you.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:12.940
It's actually the first time I've talked to a Momoto since I came to the human world.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.040
Is that so?

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:19.260
Of course. Normally you just start fighting right away until the book of the other Momoto is burned.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:22.810
Yeah, I guess so, but, uh, never mind.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:28.740
Hey, since I never get the chance to talk to a Momoto, can I ask you a question?

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:29.980
Sure, what is...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.060
In your battles, did you happen to come across a Momoto who's named Cherish?

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:35.820
Why?

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:37.960
Well, I've been looking for her for a while now.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:39.530
Her?

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.120
Yeah, she's a girl Momoto.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:42.940
Pretty, too.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.130
She's always wearing this big hat.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:48.640
Her hair smells so nice, and it's long and wavy.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:50.070
Uh...

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:51.450
Oh, no.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:56.430
Oh, thanks anyway.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:59.100
Are you friends with her?

00:07:59.420 --> 00:07:59.980
No, we're...

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:06.730
much more than friends. She's like the only family I've ever had. I never really had a mother or

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:18.250
father. She's the only one. The only one that's ever been important to me. I see. You know, my

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:25.290
memories from the Momodo world are all gone. That's why I can understand how you feel. I can't

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.970
remember having a mom or dad either. Those memories must be really important.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:49.030
to you hey hold your hands out i'm gonna give you my last gumball thanks i love gumballs thank

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:58.820
you zatch oh thank you ted what have you been up to ted

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.530
No hotel, huh? Five stars.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:06.250
Huh. Quiet, I'm working on a place to stay right now.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:07.270
Stop lying!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:07.670
Ah!

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:10.870
Being at the park must mean that you're getting ready to camp out!

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:14.200
Eh, lying!

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:16.530
Huh?

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:17.810
This place!

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:18.910
Huh?

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:25.420
I wonder whose bike this is.

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:27.400
I'm home!

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:28.440
Hi, son!

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:29.970
It appears...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:41.970
We have guests with us tonight. That's that makes friends so easily

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.780
Good evening

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:56.360
Sorry for the intrusion. No, it's all right. Stop standing there like that Keo and sit down. Oh, yeah

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:08.660
This is the town where the one who has inherited Bao resides.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.470
These dishes are spotless. Ted, nice job.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:22.400
Huh? You sound surprised. Like maybe I wasn't capable of doing a good job.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:26.140
But let me tell you something. Lady, I'm a lot more capable than you think.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.420
Is that any way to talk to your hostess?

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:36.720
Wasn't she good to you?

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.540
She fed you, took care of you, let you stay the night?

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.820
I'm sorry, ma'am.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.860
Thank you for your wonderful hospitality.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.960
You're so very welcome.

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:52.410
Now, what would you like to have for breakfast tomorrow morning?

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:54.590
You mean I get breakfast, too?

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:55.730
Of course.

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:56.740
Wow.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:57.680
Let's see.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.520
Hey, can you make me an omelet?

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.630
And it's not burnt black, though.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.720
Oh, boy, I really love omelets.

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:14.300
Here, Gito, use this room.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.970
I feel bad dropping it out of the blue like this.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:22.310
And the blankets are in...

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:23.970
